<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-22">22 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">US amateurs beat the Soviet Union in the 'Miracle on Ice'</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A team of American college players defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a>, four-time Olympic champions, 4-3 at the Lake Placid Winter Olympics. The US went on to win the gold medal.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/henck-arron" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/henck-arron.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/february-25">25 February</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Sergeants led by Dési Bouterse overthrow Suriname's government</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A group of 16 sergeants of the Surinamese Armed Forces, led by Dési Bouterse, overthrew the government of Prime Minister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henck-arron">Henck Arron</a> in a violent coup. It began a military <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dictatorship">dictatorship</a> that ruled the country until 1991, with summary executions of opponents.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/suriname">Suriname</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/desi-bouterse">Dési Bouterse</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henck-arron">Henck Arron</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-27">27 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mount St Helens erupts for the first time in 123 years</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A steam explosion blasted a crater in the summit of the Washington volcano after a week of earthquakes. On 18 May a massive eruption tore away its north face and killed 57 people.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-18">18 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Mount St Helens erupts in Washington State</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">An earthquake triggered a vast landslide and lateral blast that tore away the mountain's north face. Fifty-seven people died in the deadliest eruption in US history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-1">1 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">CNN launches as the first 24-hour news channel</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Ted Turner's Cable News Network began broadcasting from Atlanta. Its round-the-clock coverage created the modern continuous news cycle.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-22">22 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Iraq invades Iran</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saddam-hussein">Saddam Hussein</a>'s forces invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, starting an eight-year war of trenches, missile attacks and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poison-gas">poison gas</a>. Hundreds of thousands died before a ceasefire in 1988 left borders unchanged.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/december-8">8 December</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">John Lennon is shot dead in New York</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Mark <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Chapman shot John Lennon outside the Dakota building in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manhattan">Manhattan</a>. The killing of the former Beatle prompted vigils around the world.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/mariel-boatlift" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mariel-boatlift.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/mariel-boatlift">Mariel boatlift</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Mariel boatlift was the mass emigration of about 125,000 Cubans from the port of Mariel to Florida between April and October 1980.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/eradication-of-smallpox">Eradication of smallpox</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The global eradication of smallpox was certified by the World Health Organization in May 1980, after vaccination campaigns throughout the 19th and 20th centuries.</p></div></li></ol></section>
