<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/suriname"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Suriname.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Suriname</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Sergeants led by Desi Bouterse seize power in a coup</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-el-salvador"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20El%20Salvador.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of El Salvador</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Archbishop Óscar Romero is assassinated while saying mass</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/liberia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Liberia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Liberia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Samuel Doe’s coup ends True Whig Party rule</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/kingdom-of-zimbabwe"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Kingdom%20of%20Zimbabwe.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Kingdom of Zimbabwe</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Independent Zimbabwe takes its name from the ruins</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/labour-movement"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Labour%20movement.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Labour movement</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Strikes at Gdańsk’s shipyard lead to Solidarity, the first independent trade union recognised in the Soviet bloc</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-turkey"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Turkey.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Turkey</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The third military coup, after those of 1960 and 1971; the constitution still in force is approved by referendum in 1982.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/socialist-federal-republic-of-yugoslavia"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Socialist%20Federal%20Republic%20of%20Yugoslavia.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 4 May Tito dies; a collective presidency rotating among the republics takes his place as the foreign debt mounts.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/lakota-people"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Lakota%20people.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Lakota people</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">In United States v. Sioux Nation of Indians the Supreme Court awards $122 million for the Black Hills, which the tribes refuse</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/solidarity"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Solidarity.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Solidarity</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The dismissal of Anna Walentynowicz sets off a strike at the Gdańsk Shipyard, and the government signs the agreement allowing Solidarity to exist</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/hindutva"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Hindutva.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Hindutva</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Bharatiya Janata Party is founded</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/great-zimbabwe"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Great%20Zimbabwe.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Great Zimbabwe</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The newly independent country was named after the site and kept the soapstone bird as a national symbol</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/city/mohenjo-daro"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mohenjo-daro.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mohenjo-daro</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">UNESCO designates the site a World Heritage Site and an agreement to fund restoration is made</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/sistine-chapel-ceiling"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Sistine%20Chapel%20ceiling.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Sistine Chapel ceiling</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A restoration began with the lunettes, after preliminary tests in 1979</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/todai-ji"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/T%C5%8Ddai-ji.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Tōdai-ji</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A second large-scale restoration, begun in 1974 and using steel framing, was completed</span></li></ul></section>
